#### FUNCTION MANIPUALTE ARRAY

## GREP : 
--> In list context, return an array of element that match 
  
  @newarr = grep { $_ >= xxx && $_ <= yyy} @arr
  @newarr = grep /x/, @arr

--> In hash context
  $_ is the element of the input array
  @newarr = grep { $_ >= xxx || $hash{$_} < yyy } keys %hash 

--> In scalar context. return the number of times the expression was true
  number of the element of the array that pass the condition
  $scalar = @arr

## SPLICE -> make change to the input arr
  splice(@arr, start, length, replacement)
      cut the element in the @arr and replace it -> make change to the @arr 
      return the value that it cut
  splice(@arr, start, 0     , replacement)
      add the replacement to the start point 

## PUSH -> make change to the input arr
  push(@arr,$add) : add to the last of the arr -> make change to the @arr

## POP -> make change to the input arr
  pop(@arr) : remove the last element of the arr -> make change to the @arr
              return the element that it remove
   
## SHIFT -> make change to the input arr
  shift(@arr) : remove the first element of the @arr -> make change to the @arr
                return the element that it remove

## UNSHIFT -> make change to the input arr
  unshift(@arr, $add) : add to the first element of the arr

## JOIN 
  join (delimiter, list type) : join all element in the array using delimiter and 
                                return a scalar varible - a string

## SPLIT
  split (delimiter, scalar type) : split the scalar (string) into array using delimiter
                                   return the array
## REVERSE
  reverse (@arr) : reverse all elements in arr -> return the new array after reversed
## MAP
  @newarr = map { $_ * ... } @arr : return a new array after the expression is done

